{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"lcd-parallel","name":"LCD 16x2 green (parallel, LiquidCrystal)","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","description":"A 16x2 character LCD (HD44780) with green text, wired the classic parallel way: RS, E and four data pins, as in Arduino's LiquidCrystal examples. Includes LiquidCrystal.h for sketches. Needs its contrast pin (V0) set, like the real one.","category":"Displays","code":"// HD44780 character LCD, wired in parallel. How it works (and how this file copies it):\n//  - The board puts RS (0 = command, 1 = character) and the data pins at some levels, then pulses E.\n//    The LCD takes the data when E goes from HIGH to LOW. So this file listens to every pin change in\n//    order (edges), keeps the level of each pin, and acts on each falling E.\n//  - It starts in 8-bit mode (all of D0-D7 read at once). A \"function set\" command with DL = 0 puts\n//    it in 4-bit mode: then each byte comes as two E pulses on D4-D7, high half first. (Sketches send\n//    0x3, 0x3, 0x3, 0x2 at start-up to get there from any state; that works here too.)\n//  - Characters go into its memory (DDRAM): line 1 at 0x00-0x27, line 2 at 0x40-0x67; the screen shows\n//    16 of each, from the shift position.\n//  - Real-life details that make or break a real one: V0 sets the contrast (near 0 V = dark text;\n//    left unwired = nothing visible), RW must be LOW to write, the backlight is a separate LED (A, K).\nbench.device('hd44780', (part) => {\n  const screen = part.screen('text');\n  const ddram = new Array(128).fill(0x20);\n  let ac = 0, inc = true, displayOn = false, shift = 0, fourBit = false, half = null, cgram = false;\n  let powered = false, writes = 0, contrast = 0, lit = false, rwHigh = false;\n  const level = { RS: 0, RW: 0, E: 0, D0: 1, D1: 1, D2: 1, D3: 1, D4: 0, D5: 0, D6: 0, D7: 0 };\n\n  const reset = () => {\n    ddram.fill(0x20);\n    ac = 0; inc = true; displayOn = false; shift = 0; fourBit = false; half = null; cgram = false;\n  };\n  // the HD44780's instruction set (datasheet table 6)\n  const command = (c) => {\n    if (c & 0x80) { ac = c & 0x7f; cgram = false; }            // set DDRAM address (setCursor)\n    else if (c & 0x40) cgram = true;                           // set CGRAM address (createChar): not drawn\n    else if (c & 0x20) { fourBit = !(c & 0x10); half = null; } // function set: DL bit\n    else if (c & 0x10) {                                       // cursor / display shift\n      if (c & 0x08) shift += c & 0x04 ? -1 : 1;\n      else ac = (ac + (c & 0x04 ? 1 : -1)) & 0x7f;\n    } else if (c & 0x08) displayOn = !!(c & 0x04);             // display on/off\n    else if (c & 0x04) inc = !!(c & 0x02);                     // entry mode\n    else if (c & 0x02) { ac = 0; shift = 0; }                  // home\n    else if (c & 0x01) { ddram.fill(0x20); ac = 0; shift = 0; inc = true; } // clear\n  };\n  const data = (d) => {\n    if (cgram) return;\n    ddram[ac] = d;\n    ac = (ac + (inc ? 1 : -1)) & 0x7f;\n  };\n  const bits = (pins) => pins.reduce((v, p, i) => v | ((level[p] ? 1 : 0) << i), 0);\n  /** E fell: take what's on the data pins */\n  const latch = () => {\n    if (!powered || rwHigh) return;\n    writes++;\n    if (!fourBit) {\n      const v = bits(['D0', 'D1', 'D2', 'D3', 'D4', 'D5', 'D6', 'D7']);\n      return level.RS ? data(v) : command(v);\n    }\n    const nibble = bits(['D4', 'D5', 'D6', 'D7']);\n    if (half === null) { half = nibble; return; }\n    const v = (half << 4) | nibble;\n    half = null;\n    level.RS ? data(v) : command(v);\n  };\n  const line = (start) => {\n    let s = '';\n    for (let c = 0; c < 16; c++) {\n      const code = ddram[(start + (((c + shift) % 40) + 40) % 40) & 0x7f];\n      s += code >= 0x20 && code < 0x7f ? String.fromCharCode(code) : code < 8 ? '█' : '?';\n    }\n    return s;\n  };\n\n  return {\n    // every pin change the board made, in order: [['RS', 1], ['D4', 0], ['E', 1], ['E', 0], ...]\n    edges(events) {\n      for (const [pin, v] of events) {\n        const wasE = level.E;\n        if (pin in level) level[pin] = v;\n        if (pin === 'E' && wasE && !v) latch();\n      }\n    },\n    step(io) {\n      const vdd = io.supply('VDD', 'VSS');\n      const now = vdd >= 4;\n      if (now !== powered) {\n        powered = now;\n        if (!now) reset();\n      }\n      // levels as the step ends (edges keep them up to date; this catches pins changed slowly)\n      for (const p of Object.keys(level)) {\n        const l = io.level(p);\n        if (l !== null) level[p] = l;\n      }\n      rwHigh = io.level('RW') === 1;\n      // contrast: how far V0 is below VDD (about 4 V or more = full; floating = invisible)\n      const v0 = io.v('V0');\n      contrast = v0 === null ? 0 : Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (vdd - v0 - 1.5) / 2.5));\n      lit = io.supply('A', 'K') > 2.5;\n      screen.light(powered && lit);\n      const show = powered && displayOn && contrast > 0.05;\n      // faint contrast: show the characters only when it's high enough to read\n      screen.print(0, 0, show && contrast > 0.3 ? line(0x00) : ' '.repeat(16));\n      screen.print(0, 1, show && contrast > 0.3 ? line(0x40) : ' '.repeat(16));\n    },\n    status() {\n      if (!powered) return ['no power (VDD needs 5 V, VSS to GND)'];\n      const notes = [];\n      if (rwHigh) notes.push('RW is HIGH: it is in read mode and ignores writes (wire RW to GND)');\n      if (contrast <= 0.3) notes.push(contrast === 0 ? 'no contrast: V0 is not wired (put it on a knob between 5 V and GND, or on GND)' : 'contrast too low to read: turn the knob towards GND');\n      if (!lit) notes.push('backlight off (A to 5 V, K to GND)');\n      return [`${displayOn ? 'display on' : 'display off'}, ${fourBit ? '4-bit' : '8-bit'} mode, ${writes} writes`, ...notes];\n    },\n  };\n});\n","sketch":{"LiquidCrystal.h":{"classes":["LiquidCrystal"],"code":"// LiquidCrystal for sketches: Arduino's LiquidCrystal library (the constructors and functions of the\n// real one), talking to an HD44780 over its pins the same way: set RS and the data pins, pulse E.\n// Runs inside the program's thread, where pinMode, digitalWrite, delay... are in scope.\n// (The real library waits microseconds between pulses; the simulated LCD doesn't need them, so\n// they're left out except after clear/home, which take 2 ms on a real one.)\nclass LiquidCrystal {\n  // LiquidCrystal(rs, enable, d4, d5, d6, d7)            4-bit\n  // LiquidCrystal(rs, rw, enable, d4, d5, d6, d7)        4-bit with RW on a pin\n  // LiquidCrystal(rs, enable, d0, d1, ..., d7)           8-bit\n  // LiquidCrystal(rs, rw, enable, d0, d1, ..., d7)       8-bit with RW\n  constructor(...p) {\n    if (p.length === 6) [this.rs, this.rw, this.en, this.data] = [p[0], -1, p[1], p.slice(2)];\n    else if (p.length === 7) [this.rs, this.rw, this.en, this.data] = [p[0], p[1], p[2], p.slice(3)];\n    else if (p.length === 10) [this.rs, this.rw, this.en, this.data] = [p[0], -1, p[1], p.slice(2)];\n    else if (p.length === 11) [this.rs, this.rw, this.en, this.data] = [p[0], p[1], p[2], p.slice(3)];\n    else throw new Error('LiquidCrystal(rs, enable, d4, d5, d6, d7): wrong number of pins');\n    this.eightBit = this.data.length === 8;\n    this.ctrl = 0x04; // display on, cursor off, blink off\n    this.mode = 0x02; // left to right, no autoscroll\n    this.offsets = [0x00, 0x40, 0x10, 0x50];\n    this.cols = 16;\n    this.rows = 2;\n  }\n  pulse() {\n    digitalWrite(this.en, LOW);\n    digitalWrite(this.en, HIGH);\n    digitalWrite(this.en, LOW); // the LCD takes the data as E falls\n  }\n  bits(value, n) {\n    for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) digitalWrite(this.data[i], (value >> i) & 1);\n    this.pulse();\n  }\n  send(value, rs) {\n    digitalWrite(this.rs, rs);\n    if (this.rw >= 0) digitalWrite(this.rw, LOW);\n    if (this.eightBit) this.bits(value, 8);\n    else {\n      this.bits(value >> 4, 4);\n      this.bits(value & 0x0f, 4);\n    }\n  }\n  command(c) { this.send(c, LOW); }\n  begin(cols = 16, rows = 2) {\n    this.cols = cols;\n    this.rows = rows;\n    this.offsets = [0x00, 0x40, 0x00 + cols, 0x40 + cols];\n    pinMode(this.rs, OUTPUT);\n    if (this.rw >= 0) pinMode(this.rw, OUTPUT);\n    pinMode(this.en, OUTPUT);\n    for (const d of this.data) pinMode(d, OUTPUT);\n    delay(50); // power-up time\n    digitalWrite(this.rs, LOW);\n    digitalWrite(this.en, LOW);\n    if (this.rw >= 0) digitalWrite(this.rw, LOW);\n    const lines = rows > 1 ? 0x08 : 0;\n    if (!this.eightBit) {\n      // the datasheet's way into 4-bit mode, from whatever state it's in\n      this.bits(0x03, 4); delay(5);\n      this.bits(0x03, 4); delay(1);\n      this.bits(0x03, 4);\n      this.bits(0x02, 4);\n      this.command(0x20 | lines);\n    } else {\n      this.command(0x30 | lines); delay(5);\n      this.command(0x30 | lines);\n      this.command(0x30 | lines);\n    }\n    this.display();\n    this.clear();\n    this.command(0x04 | this.mode);\n  }\n  clear() { this.command(0x01); delay(2); }\n  home() { this.command(0x02); delay(2); }\n  setCursor(col, row) {\n    const r = Math.max(0, Math.min(row, this.rows - 1, 3));\n    this.command(0x80 | (col + this.offsets[r]));\n  }\n  noDisplay() { this.ctrl &= ~0x04; this.command(0x08 | this.ctrl); }\n  display() { this.ctrl |= 0x04; this.command(0x08 | this.ctrl); }\n  noCursor() { this.ctrl &= ~0x02; this.command(0x08 | this.ctrl); }\n  cursor() { this.ctrl |= 0x02; this.command(0x08 | this.ctrl); }\n  noBlink() { this.ctrl &= ~0x01; this.command(0x08 | this.ctrl); }\n  blink() { this.ctrl |= 0x01; this.command(0x08 | this.ctrl); }\n  scrollDisplayLeft() { this.command(0x18); }\n  scrollDisplayRight() { this.command(0x1c); }\n  leftToRight() { this.mode |= 0x02; this.command(0x04 | this.mode); }\n  rightToLeft() { this.mode &= ~0x02; this.command(0x04 | this.mode); }\n  autoscroll() { this.mode |= 0x01; this.command(0x04 | this.mode); }\n  noAutoscroll() { this.mode &= ~0x01; this.command(0x04 | this.mode); }\n  createChar(location, charmap) {\n    this.command(0x40 | ((location & 7) << 3));\n    for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) this.send(charmap[i] ?? 0, HIGH);\n  }\n  write(b) { this.send(Number(b) & 0xff, HIGH); return 1; }\n  print(x, f) {\n    let s;\n    if (typeof x === 'number' && f !== undefined) s = f === 16 ? x.toString(16).toUpperCase() : f === 2 ? x.toString(2) : x.toFixed(f);\n    else if (typeof x === 'number' && !Number.isInteger(x)) s = x.toFixed(2);\n    else s = String(x);\n    for (const ch of s) this.write(ch.charCodeAt(0));\n    return s.length;\n  }\n  println(x, f) { return this.print(x, f); }\n}\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"lcd1602-green","name":"LCD 16x2 green (parallel)","description":"16 pins, left to right: VSS (GND), VDD (5 V), V0 (contrast: a 10k knob between 5 V and GND, middle leg here; near 0 V = darkest text), RS, RW (to GND), E, D0-D7 (only D4-D7 in 4-bit mode), A and K (the backlight: A to 5 V, K to GND). In a sketch: #include <LiquidCrystal.h>, LiquidCrystal lcd(rs, e, d4, d5, d6, d7); lcd.begin(16, 2); lcd.print(\"Hello\");","swatch":"#2fa84f","mass":32,"shape":[{"box":[8,0.16,3.6],"at":[0,0.08,0],"color":"#1d6b3a"},{"box":[7.1,0.7,2.4],"at":[0,0.51,0.1],"color":"#1a1a1c"},{"screen":{"id":"text","size":[6.4,1.45],"px":[16,2],"mode":"text","on":"#6dff7a","off":"#04100a","bg":"#0c2414"},"at":[0,0.862,0.1]}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["VSS","VDD","V0","RS","RW","E","D0","D1","D2","D3","D4","D5","D6","D7","A","K"],"at":[-3.2,0.16,-1.55],"kinds":{"VSS":"gnd","VDD":"vin","V0":"in","RS":"in","RW":"in","E":"in","D0":"in","D1":"in","D2":"in","D3":"in","D4":"in","D5":"in","D6":"in","D7":"in","A":"in","K":"gnd"},"extra":{"VDD":{"label":"VDD (5 V)","vmin":4.5,"vmax":5.5},"V0":{"label":"V0 (contrast)"},"RW":{"label":"RW (to GND: write)"},"D0":{"pulled":"up"},"D1":{"pulled":"up"},"D2":{"pulled":"up"},"D3":{"pulled":"up"},"A":{"label":"A (backlight +)"},"K":{"label":"K (backlight -)"}}}],"device":"hd44780"}],"examples":[{"name":"Hello, LCD (LiquidCrystal)","description":"The LCD wired to a board as in Arduino's LiquidCrystal Hello World, with a knob for contrast. Press Run; turn the knob if the text is faint.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Hello, LCD (LiquidCrystal)","libraries":[{"id":"lcd-parallel","name":"LCD 16x2 green (parallel, LiquidCrystal)","version":"1.0.0"}],"parts":[{"uid":"board","type":"uno-wifi-board","name":"Board","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"lcd","type":"lcd-parallel/lcd1602-green","name":"LCD","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[0,0,-8],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"knob","type":"knob","name":"Contrast knob","params":{"start":10},"parent":null,"pos":[7,0,-3],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"VSS"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"VDD"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"RW"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND3"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"K"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"A"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"D12"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"RS"},"color":"#4f9cff"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"D11"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"E"},"color":"#ff9d3a"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"D5"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"D4"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"D4"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"D5"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"D3"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"D6"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"board","pin":"D2"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"D7"},"color":"#3fbf7f"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"knob","pin":"L"},"b":{"uid":"board","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w13","a":{"uid":"knob","pin":"H"},"b":{"uid":"board","pin":"5V"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w14","a":{"uid":"knob","pin":"W"},"b":{"uid":"lcd","pin":"V0"},"color":"#e8c547"}],"programs":{"board":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Hello, LCD: Arduino's LiquidCrystal \"Hello World\", on the bench.\n// The LCD shows a greeting on line 1 and the seconds since start on line 2.\n// Wiring (as in the Arduino example): RS -> 12, E -> 11, D4 -> 5, D5 -> 4, D6 -> 3, D7 -> 2,\n// VSS and RW and K -> GND, VDD and A -> 5V, V0 -> the knob's middle leg (its ends on 5V and GND).\n// Faint or no text? Turn the knob (right panel while running) towards GND: that's the contrast.\n#include <LiquidCrystal.h>\n\nLiquidCrystal lcd(12, 11, 5, 4, 3, 2);   // rs, enable, d4, d5, d6, d7\n\nvoid setup() {\n  lcd.begin(16, 2);          // 16 columns, 2 rows\n  lcd.print(\"Hello, world!\");\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int seconds = millis() / 1000;\n  lcd.setCursor(0, 1);       // column 0, row 1 (the second line)\n  lcd.print(seconds);\n  lcd.print(\" s\");\n  delay(250);\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}